# The design, in the DESIGN.md format

## Overview

A light page with color kept to small details and a fine film-grain texture. This file is one file of a Prescription from Refraction Studio. \`PRESCRIPTION.md\` is the instruction and decides where two files differ; \`tokens.css\` holds every value of the design, also those that this format has no place for; \`mockup.html\` is the reference page.

Fingerprint of the design values: \`68551dae\`. Every file of this Prescription carries the same eight characters; where one differs, the files do not belong together.

## Colors

The page is light. The colors below are written as the reference page draws them.

- **Primary (#c83122):** the one color that people remember. Use it where the Step “Amount of color” puts it: color in small details only (Buttons take the color of the text; the main color appears only in links and small details).
- **Background (#fefaf1) and text (#171105):** the page and its reading text. Muted text is #605848.
- **Button (#171105) with its label (#fefaf1):** the main button. The Studio measured this pair.
- **Link (#c83122):** links in running text, always underlined.
- **Borders:** rgb(23 17 5 / 0.146) for quiet lines; #766f60 for the edge of a form field.

## Typography

Headings are set in Newsreader Variable, reading text in Instrument Sans Variable. \`FONTS.md\` says how to ship them. The largest headline grows with the window; this file gives its largest size, and \`tokens.css\` holds the exact rule under \`--text-display\`.

## Layout

The page is at most 68rem wide. Spacing follows the named steps in \`tokens.css\` (\`--space-1\` to \`--space-32\`); use no spacing that is not one of them.

- Menu: links in a left column (A fixed column on the left holds the name and the links; content scrolls beside it).
- First screen: very large headline (A very large headline across the full width, with the paragraph and buttons in a row beneath a rule).
- List of services: numbered list beside a fixed title (The section title stays fixed on the left while a numbered list scrolls on the right).

## Elevation & Depth

Boxes stand apart from the page like this: thin outlines (Thin outlines; no shadows). The exact shadows and edges are in \`tokens.css\` (\`--card-shadow\`, \`--card-border\`); this format has no place for a shadow.

## Shapes

Buttons and fields are rounded by 2px, boxes by 3px, small marks by 1px. A field of several lines inside a box is never rounder than the box.

## Components

- **Main button:** the button color with its label color, 2.75rem tall at least, rounded as above. On press and on focus it behaves as section 4 of \`PRESCRIPTION.md\` says.
- **Field:** the surface color, the strong border, the same rounding and least height as the button.
- **Card:** the card color, rounded as a box.

## Do's and Don'ts

- Do use the names in \`tokens.css\`; do not write a raw color, size, or spacing into a component.
- Do build to match \`mockup.html\`, and compare your page with it before you report.
- Don't load a font, a script, or a style sheet from another site.
- Don't mark anything by color alone: a link is underlined, and an error has a mark and words.
- Don't drift toward “Name left, links right” or “Name centered, links below” or “Links centered, button right” on “Menu (navigation)”: the owner saw them and chose otherwise.
"
`;

exports[`The Prescription, first slice (SPEC.md section 2.6) > writes FONTS.md: each typeface with its family, licence, package, and version, and a device’s own typeface without a file (SPEC.md section 2.9) > a worked project: FONTS.md 1`] = `
"# Fonts for this design

This file belongs to a Prescription from Refraction Studio. It tells an AI coding tool, and the owner, which typefaces the design uses and how the built site ships them.

Fingerprint of the design values: \`68551dae\`. Every file of this Prescription carries the same eight characters; where one differs, the files do not belong together.

## Rules

1. Ship every font file from the site’s own address. Load no font from another site: no font service, no content delivery network.
2. Use the variable file of a typeface: one file holds every weight.
3. Write \`font-display: swap\`, so that text shows at once in a fallback and changes when the file has arrived.
4. Keep each typeface’s licence text with its files. The packages below hold it.
5. The files named here hold the Latin letters. A site in another script needs that script’s file from the same package.

## The typefaces

### Newsreader (headings)

- CSS family: \`Newsreader Variable\`
- Fallbacks, in order: \`Georgia\`, \`Times New Roman\`, \`serif\`
- Licence: OFL-1.1 (the SIL Open Font License: free to use, to ship, and to change; the licence text stays with the files).
- Package: \`@fontsource-variable/newsreader\`, version 5.3.0. This is the version that the Studio itself ships, so its files are the ones that the preview drew.
- File in the package: \`files/newsreader-latin-wght-normal.woff2\`

\`\`\`css
@font-face {
  font-family: "Newsreader Variable";
  src: url("/fonts/newsreader-latin-wght-normal.woff2") format("woff2");
  font-weight: 200 800;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
\`\`\`

### Instrument Sans (reading text)

- CSS family: \`Instrument Sans Variable\`
- Fallbacks, in order: \`system-ui\`, \`-apple-system\`, \`Segoe UI\`, \`Roboto\`, \`sans-serif\`
- Licence: OFL-1.1 (the SIL Open Font License: free to use, to ship, and to change; the licence text stays with the files).
- Package: \`@fontsource-variable/instrument-sans\`, version 5.3.0. This is the version that the Studio itself ships, so its files are the ones that the preview drew.
- File in the package: \`files/instrument-sans-latin-wght-normal.woff2\`

\`\`\`css
@font-face {
  font-family: "Instrument Sans Variable";
  src: url("/fonts/instrument-sans-latin-wght-normal.woff2") format("woff2");
  font-weight: 400 700;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
\`\`\`

The address \`/fonts/\` is an example: put the files where the site keeps its own files, and write that address.
"
`;

exports[`The Prescription, first slice (SPEC.md section 2.6) > writes theme.css: every name that the shadcn component library reads, each with a value of the design, the same for the light and the dark name (SPEC.md section 2.9) > a worked project: theme.css 1`] = `
"/* The design of one Refraction project, under the names that the shadcn component library reads. Fingerprint: 68551dae.
   Put these two blocks where the project keeps the library's theme (its main style sheet), in place of the library's own values.
   tokens.css holds every value of the design under the design's own names; this file holds the part that the library has names for.

   The design is a light page and has one set of colors. The dark name holds the same values as the light one, so that
   the page looks the same whichever of the two the library switches on.
   --radius is the rounding of boxes. The design rounds buttons and fields by --radius-control in tokens.css; give them that.
   --destructive: the design draws an error in the color of the text, with a mark and words, and never by color alone.
   --chart-1 to --chart-5: the design has no palette for charts. These are five of its own colors; a chart needs a palette
   that a person has looked at. */
:root {
  --radius: 3px;
  --background: #fefaf1;
  --foreground: #171105;
  --card: #ffffff;
  --card-foreground: #171105;
  --popover: #ffffff;
  --popover-foreground: #171105;
  --primary: #171105;
  --primary-foreground: #fefaf1;
  --secondary: #f5f0e5;
  --secondary-foreground: #171105;
  --muted: #f5f0e5;
  --muted-foreground: #605848;
  --accent: #f5f0e5;
  --accent-foreground: #171105;
  --destructive: #171105;
  --border: rgb(23 17 5 / 0.146);
  --input: #766f60;
  --ring: #c83122;
  --chart-1: #c83122;
  --chart-2: #c83122;
  --chart-3: #605848;
  --chart-4: #766f60;
  --chart-5: #171105;
  --sidebar: #f5f0e5;
  --sidebar-foreground: #171105;
  --sidebar-primary: #171105;
  --sidebar-primary-foreground: #fefaf1;
  --sidebar-accent: #f5f0e5;
  --sidebar-accent-foreground: #171105;
  --sidebar-border: rgb(23 17 5 / 0.146);
  --sidebar-ring: #c83122;
}

.dark {
  --radius: 3px;
  --background: #fefaf1;
  --foreground: #171105;
  --card: #ffffff;
  --card-foreground: #171105;
  --popover: #ffffff;
  --popover-foreground: #171105;
  --primary: #171105;
  --primary-foreground: #fefaf1;
  --secondary: #f5f0e5;
  --secondary-foreground: #171105;
  --muted: #f5f0e5;
  --muted-foreground: #605848;
  --accent: #f5f0e5;
  --accent-foreground: #171105;
  --destructive: #171105;
  --border: rgb(23 17 5 / 0.146);
  --input: #766f60;
  --ring: #c83122;
  --chart-1: #c83122;
  --chart-2: #c83122;
  --chart-3: #605848;
  --chart-4: #766f60;
  --chart-5: #171105;
  --sidebar: #f5f0e5;
  --sidebar-foreground: #171105;
  --sidebar-primary: #171105;
  --sidebar-primary-foreground: #fefaf1;
  --sidebar-accent: #f5f0e5;
  --sidebar-accent-foreground: #171105;
  --sidebar-border: rgb(23 17 5 / 0.146);
  --sidebar-ring: #c83122;
}
"
`;
